# Rule: web (Next.js App Router, TypeScript), in `<%webDir%>/`

## Layout
```
src/app/            routes (server components by default), layout, globals.css, tokens.css (generated)
src/components/     presentational components: props in, JSX out, no data fetching
<%#hasBackend%>
src/lib/            typed API client (mirrors .ai/contract/openapi.json), helpers
<%/hasBackend%>
<%^hasBackend%>
src/lib/            data access and helpers: plain functions a server component calls
<%/hasBackend%>
src/__tests__/      Vitest + Testing Library specs
```

## Conventions
- TypeScript `strict` (+ `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`). No `any`; narrow `unknown` with type guards at the boundary.
<%#hasBackend%>
- All backend access goes through `src/lib/api.ts`. Never call `fetch` from a component. Responses are validated against the contract shape before use.
- `API_URL` is a RUNTIME variable (server-side). Never bake environment-specific URLs into the build: one image runs in every environment.
<%/hasBackend%>
<%^hasBackend%>
- This app has no separate backend. Server-side work lives in server components and route handlers (`src/app/api/<name>/route.ts`), and calls plain functions from `src/lib/`. Never call `fetch` from a component.
- Treat everything that comes in (query strings, request bodies, cookies) as `unknown` and validate it at the boundary before use.
- Configuration is read from environment variables at request time, never baked into the build: one image runs in every environment.
<%/hasBackend%>
- Every data-driven view models all its states explicitly: loading, empty, error, success. Errors are shown with `role="alert"`, never swallowed.
- Prefer server components for data; add `"use client"` only for interactivity, and keep it as low in the tree as possible.
- Styling: every colour, space, radius and size is a design token, written `var(--color-accent)`, `var(--space-md)`, ... Never a literal value. `src/app/tokens.css` is generated from `.ai/design/tokens.json` (`./<%sdlcDir%>/sdlc design sync`): never edit it. Rule: `.ai/rules/design.md`.
- Accessibility: semantic elements, labelled controls, visible focus, sufficient contrast. Don't convey state by colour alone.
- Lint with `eslint --max-warnings 0` (flat config, `eslint-config-next`); fix the code instead of adding `eslint-disable`. React Compiler rules apply: no JSX construction inside `try/catch` (compute props in the `try`, render outside it).

## Tests (Vitest, coverage floor <%coverageWeb%>%)
- Test behaviour through the rendered output (`getByRole`, `getByText`), not implementation details.
<%#hasBackend%>
- Server components are async functions: `render(await Page())`, with `fetchHello` mocked at the module boundary.
- Cover each state of each component and each error path of `src/lib/api.ts`.

## Contract
When the backend contract changes, update `src/lib/api.ts` types and tests in the same PR.
<%/hasBackend%>
<%^hasBackend%>
- Server components are async functions: `render(await HomePage({ searchParams: Promise.resolve({}) }))`.
- Test pure logic in `src/lib/` directly, without rendering. Cover each state of each component and each rejected input.
<%/hasBackend%>
